[[- if .Inertia]]

# Pages, forms and components

1. **The page and its props** (`app/handlers`): a struct of the props,
   and the page, declared once with its component:

   ```go
   type ReportProps struct {
   	Rows []ReportRow `json:"rows"`
   }

   var reportPage = page[ReportProps]("Reports/Show") // frontend/src/pages/Reports/Show[[.Ext]]
   ```

   The handler renders it: `return reportPage.Render(c, ReportProps{…})`,
   or, in a typed handler (`web.H`), `return reportPage.Responder(props), nil`.
2. **The types:** `go run . types` (which `go tool anetos dev` runs)
   writes `frontend/src/types/pages.ts`, with [[if eq .Framework "vue"]]the props' type (`ReportProps`,
   which the component takes with `defineProps<ReportProps>()`; the
   shared props come from `usePage().props`)[[else]]`PageProps<'Reports/Show'>`[[end]],
   and `routes.ts`, with `route(name, params)`. Never write those types
   by hand.
3. **The component** (`frontend/src/pages/Reports/Show[[.Ext]]`): built
   from the components of `[[.UI]]` (`PageHeader`,
   `Card`, `Field`, `Input`, `Button`, `Table`…), **no CSS classes in
   pages**: to change the look, change a component there or
   `src/theme.css`. The layout (`src/Layout[[.Ext]]`) wraps every page.
   Text comes from `locales/en/*.yaml` through `useT()`
   (`t('reports.title')`), numbers and dates through `useFormat()`; links
   are Inertia's `Link` to `route('reports.show', { id })`.
4. **The route** in `routes/web.go` (or the resource's file):
   `pages.Get("/reports", h.Index).Name("reports.index")`, in the page
   group, which has sessions, CSRF protection and Inertia's middleware.
5. **A form:** Inertia's [[if eq .Framework "vue"]]`<Form :action="route('reports.create')" method="post">`[[else]]`<Form action={route('reports.create')} method="post">`[[end]];
   the CSRF token goes in a header by itself. The handler takes an input
   struct with `validate` tags; on a validation error Inertia goes back to
   the form, whose `errors` hold the messages by field. JSON binding is
   strict: turn checkboxes and numbers into booleans and numbers in the
   form's `transform`.
6. Test with `app.Get("/reports").AssertInertia("Reports/Show")` and
   `.AssertInertiaProp("rows.0.title", "…")`. Then `go tool anetos check`,
   and `go tool anetos build`, which type-checks the frontend.

Docs: `go tool anetos docs guides/inertia`, `go tool anetos docs guides/typescript`,
`go tool anetos docs guides/forms`.
[[- else]]

# Pages, forms and components

1. **The handler** (`go tool anetos make:handler Reports`, or a method
   on an existing one) renders a templ component:
   `return c.Render(http.StatusOK, views.Report(data))`, or, in a typed handler
   (`web.H`), `return web.Render(views.Report(data)), nil`.
[[- if .HasUI]]
2. **The view** (`views/report.templ`): call the layout and the
   components of `views/ui` (`@ui.PageHeader`, `@ui.Card`, `@ui.Button`,
   `@ui.Form`, `@ui.Field`, `@ui.Table`…). **No CSS classes outside `views/ui`**: to
   change the look, change a component there (or `go tool anetos css:use`
   to switch frameworks).
[[- else]]
2. **The view** (`views/report.templ`): call the layout, and follow the
   markup and classes of the existing pages and `public/static/app.css`.
[[- end]] Text comes from `locales/en/*.yaml`
   (`i18n.T(ctx, "reports.title")`).
3. **The route** in `routes/web.go` (or the resource's file):
   `pages.Get("/reports", h.Index).Name("reports.index")`, in the page
   group, which has sessions and CSRF protection.
4. **A form:** `@view.CSRFField(ctx)` inside it; the handler takes an
   input struct with `validate` tags; on a validation error the form
   comes back with the errors (`view.Errors(ctx)`) and the input
   (`view.Old(ctx, …)`). PUT and DELETE: `@view.MethodField("PUT")`.
5. `go tool templ generate` runs in `go tool anetos dev` and `check`.
   Then `go tool anetos check`.

Docs: `go tool anetos docs guides/views`, `go tool anetos docs guides/forms`,
`go tool anetos docs reference/ui` (every component),
`go tool anetos docs guides/styling`.
[[- end]]
